  "rules": [
    "Model exhibits severe upward bias when recent history shows a strong downtrend (e.g., dropping from ~79 to ~63) followed by a spike; forecasts consistently overshoot the true peak by 5-10%.",
    "Forecasts fail to capture immediate mean reversion after volatility spikes, instead projecting a smooth linear recovery that ignores sudden reversals.",
    "Sentiment history (values > 0.20) correlates with forecast stability but does not prevent over-smoothing of sharp price swings in the first 5-7 days of the horizon.",
    "When sentiment is near zero and volatility is high, the model underestimates the probability of a V-shaped recovery or crash within the first week.",
    "The model assumes monotonic trends where true outcomes are characterized by erratic, non-linear movements driven by market shocks."
  ]
}
